course: dictionary
lesson: 14208
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. The word muff is a good example. Read the whole sentence before you decide what a word means.
explain: «Grandma kept her hands warm inside a soft fur muff.» Here a muff is a tube of fur that you put both hands into. «Sam wore ear muffs at the fireworks to block out the loud bangs.» Here muffs are two soft pads on a band, worn over the ears.
explain: «Ella was sure she would catch the ball, but she muffed it.» Here muffed is a verb, an action word. It means she did it badly and missed the catch. Ask yourself: is the word a thing, or is it something someone does?
fact: A muff (noun) is a soft tube of fur or warm cloth that you put both hands into to keep them warm.
fact: Ear muffs (noun) are two soft pads joined by a band, worn to keep your ears warm or to block out loud noise.
fact: To muff (verb) means to do something badly or miss it, such as dropping an easy catch.
fact: Phrases you may hear: «muff a catch», «muff it» and «muff your lines», all meaning to spoil a chance or get something wrong.
fact: A good check: swap your meaning into the sentence. If «missed it» fits, the verb meaning is right.
exercise: «Mia put her hands inside the soft fur muff to keep them warm.» What is a muff in this sentence? | A kind of football goal | A loud noise made by a machine | *A soft tube of fur for keeping hands warm
exercise: «The fireworks were loud, so Sam wore ear muffs.» What do ear muffs do? | Make hair grow thicker | *Keep ears warm or block out loud noise | Help you swim faster
exercise: «Ella was sure to catch the ball, but she muffed it.» What does muffed mean? | Ran off with the ball | *Did it badly and missed it | Threw it far away | Caught it very neatly
test: «Tom will muff his lines if he rushes the poem.» What does muff mean here? | *Mess up by forgetting or getting it wrong | Put on warm gloves | Read the poem very loudly
test: «The old lady's fur muff kept her hands toasty in the snow.» Which meaning fits muff here? | To miss a catch | A type of winter hat | *A soft tube of fur to keep hands warm | Two pads worn over the ears
exam: «Jo watched the ball, then muffed the catch and sighed.» What does muffed mean? | *Did it badly and missed it | Threw it hard across the field | Kicked it far into the goal | Caught it cleanly
